## ✅ Advantages & Limitations

**Advantages:**
```
✓ Fast training and prediction
✓ Works with high-dimensional data
✓ Few parameters (linear)
✓ Probabilistic: Get confidence scores
✓ Handles multiclass naturally
✓ Works well with small datasets
✓ Easy to implement
✓ Good baseline classifier
```

**Limitations:**
```
✗ Naive independence assumption often violated
✗ May be outperformed by complex models
✗ Feature correlated → biased probabilities
✗ Zero probability problem (needs smoothing)
✗ Can't learn feature interactions
✗ Assumes feature distributions
✗ Not good for truly continuous features
```

