## 🎯 QUICK REFERENCE DECISION TREES

### Choose ML Algorithm By Problem Type

```
REGRESSION (Predict continuous value):
├─ Simple, few features → Linear Regression
├─ Non-linear relationship → Polynomial/LASSO/Ridge
├─ Many features → Ridge/LASSO (regularization)
└─ Tree-based → Decision Tree, Random Forest

BINARY CLASSIFICATION (Yes/No):
├─ Few features, fast needed → Logistic Regression
├─ Complex boundaries → SVM, Random Forest
├─ Text/high-dim → Naive Bayes, Logistic Regression
└─ Unknown structure → Try SVM with RBF kernel

MULTI-CLASS CLASSIFICATION (3+ classes):
├─ Probabilistic → Naive Bayes
├─ Any → Random Forest, SVM (one-vs-rest)
├─ Neural networks available → Neural Network
└─ Interpretability important → Decision Tree

CLUSTERING (Group similar data):
├─ Know number k → K-Means
├─ Arbitrary shapes → DBSCAN
├─ Hierarchical structure → Hierarchical Clustering
└─ Large scale → K-Means, DBSCAN
