## 🔍 DEBUGGING CHECKLIST

### Model Not Learning

```
□ Check data quality:
  - Missing values?
  - Wrong data types?
  - Features in right range?

□ Check preprocessing:
  - Features normalized?
  - Categorical features encoded?
  - Train/test properly split?

□ Check learning rate:
  - Too high: Loss diverges
  - Too low: Loss decreases very slowly
  - Try 0.001, 0.01, 0.1

□ Check model capacity:
  - Too simple: High bias
  - Too complex: High variance
  - Increase/decrease layers/features

□ Check training loop:
  - Weights updated? (check gradients)
  - Loss computed correctly?
  - Convergence criteria met?

□ Check regularization:
  - Too much: Underfitting
  - Too little: Overfitting
  - Adjust λ

□ Check data-model mismatch:
  - Linear model on nonlinear data?
  - Regression model on classification?
  - Wrong output shape?
```

### Model Overfitting

```
□ Get more data (usually best)
□ Reduce model complexity:
  - Fewer layers (NN)
  - Max depth (Trees)
  - Increase regularization (Ridge/LASSO)
  - Fewer features (feature selection)

□ Increase regularization:
  - Ridge: Add λΣw²
  - Dropout: Randomly disable units
  - Early stopping: Stop before overfitting

□ Augment data:
  - Images: Rotations, flips, crops
  - Text: Synonyms, back-translation
  - General: Add noise

□ Ensemble methods:
  - Random Forest instead of Decision Tree
  - Boosting (XGBoost, LightGBM)
  - Multiple models voted
```

