## 📈 METRICS INTERPRETATION GUIDE

### Classification Metrics

```
Accuracy = (TP + TN) / Total
- Overall correctness
- Misleading with imbalanced data

Precision = TP / (TP + FP)
- Of positives predicted, how many correct?
- "When model says yes, how often right?"
- Minimize false alarms

Recall = TP / (TP + FN)
- Of actual positives, how many found?
- "Did we find all positives?"
- Minimize missed cases

F1 Score = 2 × (Precision × Recall) / (Precision + Recall)
- Harmonic mean of precision/recall
- Good for imbalanced data

ROC-AUC:
- Trade-off between TPR and FPR
- Higher is better (0.5 = random, 1.0 = perfect)
- Good for ranking quality

Confusion Matrix:
```
              Predicted
         Positive | Negative
Actual ---|---------|----------
Positive  |   TP   |   FN   (Miss)
Negative  |   FP   |   TN
        (False alarm)
```

### Regression Metrics

```
R² = 1 - (SS_res / SS_tot)
- Proportion of variance explained
- 0: Model no better than mean
- 1: Perfect fit
- Can be negative (worse than mean)

RMSE = √(Σ(y_actual - y_pred)² / n)
- Average error magnitude
- Same units as y
- Sensitive to outliers

MAE = Σ|y_actual - y_pred| / n
- Average absolute error
- Robust to outliers
- Less sensitive to large errors

MAPE = Σ|y_actual - y_pred| / |y_actual| / n
- Percentage error
- Good for different scales
- Unstable when y ≈ 0
```

